ergy.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-85-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7076009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7a18a6340537ca70d4ab1bdb5bf535326b7ea1e31a3ba8f3ca0a0fc3fdf28b13","compact":"43612e7022dd18e75bfaeeecc62c248478aafc8b56d4ec7688ccef6deba8474b","nasal":"43612e7022dd18e75bfaeeecc62c248478aafc8b56d4ec7688ccef6deba8474b"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-76-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":76,"verse":10,"english":"There upon the highly powerful immortals headed by Indra entered the forest where the great Asura Vſtra was performing austerities.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.885,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-85-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7076010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b26c37a6e3d2286f69ac7d10ee29fadc811d8f07363fb02d8c4cc298f83ad72e","compact":"c8b6ba5d7b46b25e06284149b2a496d11100fd3f5311d3ea6f66891c740c976a","nasal":"c8b6ba5d7b46b25e06284149b2a496d11100fd3f5311d3ea6f66891c740c976a"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-76-11","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":76,"verse":11,"english":"Arriving there they observed that the leading Asura was spreading rays all over, the outcome of his own effulgence, as if devouring the three worlds and burning down the quarters.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.765,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-85-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7076011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"256d6dc383561d8e188d3d244706e874501eed5197c0f5de4507d38e13ab8c62","compact":"8c0cadf8d6dd731c8add63aa91cbec74eeef913d0f6d53d6eb3c83d8341a9796","nasal":"f0f5c72e2384197137a899d9a1e612d06fb60cdd844f06f27d20d97e2d63974e"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-76-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","s